the San Diego comic-con was awash with  superhero TV and film reveals so let's  wade through the tides like Aquaman and  go over the biggest DC and Warner  Brothers news from the show Warner  Brothers kick things off with the first  trailer for Wonder Woman the trailer  highlights the relationship between gal  gadot's diana prince and chris pine's  Steve Trevor after the latter washes up  on the shores of their mascara from what  we've seen it seems the film will be set  sometime around 1916 during the height  of World War one directed by Patty  Jenkins who also directed 2008  critically acclaimed monster starring  Charlize Theron Wonder Woman will  release June twenty-first next year DC's  answer to the Avengers the Justice  League got its first trailer and it is a  doozy confirming earlier reports that  the film would be much lighter in tone  than Batman vs Superman the trailer sees  Bruce Wayne recruiting the Warriors he  needs to battle an enemy he believes is  coming there's a better look at jason  momoa as Arthur curry aka Aquaman ray  Fisher's cyborg and Ezra Miller's  wisecracking flash the latter has  probably the best moment of the trailer  when in order to test his reflexes Bruce  Wayne Hills a Batarang at the speedster  Justice League will hit theaters on  november seventeenth 2017 in a little  under two weeks we'll finally get to see  Suicide Squad when it releases on august  five but in the mean time warner  brothers in DC released a final trailer  for the upcoming supervillain movie the  trailer showcases the team's dynamic  opening with will smith's Deadshot  reminding them that they're the patsies  they're too bad guys we then see  snippets of the main members including  Harley Quinn killer croc Captain  Boomerang katana and El Diablo Suicide  Squad follows a gang of super villains  who are coerced into taking dangerous  missions in exchange for reduced  sentences the film has been reported to  potentially take in 140 million dollars  in the US for 